// Targeted therapy: HIV provirus excision from latently infected CD4+ T cells.
//
// The virus carries the drug to where the disease hides.
//   Vector: AAV carrying dual CRISPR guides
//   Target: HIV LTR sequences flanking the integrated provirus
//   Tissue: CD4+ T cells (the latent HIV reservoir)
//
// How the sequence acts as the drug trigger:
//   1. AAV delivers Cas9 + dual LTR guides to CD4+ T cells
//   2. In cells WITHOUT integrated HIV: guides find no target → no effect
//   3. In cells WITH integrated HIV: both guides cut flanking LTRs → provirus excised
//   4. Excised cell is cured — no more viral rebound from that cell
//
// This is the "shock-free cure" approach: instead of activating latent virus
// and killing reactivated cells (shock-and-kill), you remove the virus
// from resting cells without ever waking it up.
//
// Real work: Excision BioTherapeutics EBT-101, NCT05144386 (Phase 1/2)
// Kaminski et al. 2016, Dash et al. 2019

target HIVProvirus {
  organism human
  tolerance 0
  signatures all [ ATCCAGTGCTAGCTTGA, TGACCGTAACTGCAATC ]
  in only [ cd4.t.cell ] @measured(human)
}

excise HIVProvirus
